{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/143699-new-custom-merit-contract-s-sympathy","id":143699,"title":"New Custom Merit: Contract's Sympathy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-20T10:49:57-07:00","id":143699,"title":"New Custom Merit: Contract's Sympathy","content":"Hi all,<br /> <br /> Here is a little Merit I created for my chronicles, I wanted you to give your advises on it.<br /> <br /> <b>Contract's Sympathy (ooo, Specify Contracts)</b><br /> <u>Prerequisite:</u> You must have an Affinity and at least 2 dots in the Contracts you want to gain the Sympathy. You can't have more Contract's Sympathy Merits than your score in Wyrd.<br /> <u>Effect:</u> Choose a Contract. You add your rating in the Contracts to the dice pool to activate its Clauses.<br /> <u>Drawback:</u> When you acquire a Sympathy from a Contract, you lose at the same time the chance to gain the attention of anothers. Each time you buy the Contract's Sympathy Merit, you lose access and all dots in the Affinity Contracts of another Seeming or Court (the experience points are refund). The Contracts you lose must be from the same &quot;realm&quot; that the one you got a Sympathy for (Seeming for Seeming and Court for Court). You can't ban the same Contracts for two different Sympathy. <i>Example: Belle, a Spring Fairest, acquire a Sympathy with the Contracts of Fleeting Spring. She chooses to forgot her Clauses with the Affinity Contracts of the Summer Court, losing all her dots in the Contracts of Eternal Summer and the Contracts of Fleeting Summer and forever banned to learned them.</i><br /> <br /> So, overpowered? Underpriced? Good enough?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":822,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/822-daemonchrno","user":"DaemonChrno","date":". 05-20-2014, 02:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/822-daemonchrno","name":"DaemonChrno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar822_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T11:47:16-07:00","id":143746,"title":"","content":"I think it's an interesting way to allow for some min/maxing. I would suggest that it is a type of Goblin Contract rather than a merit, though.<br /> <br /> If you are interested in toning down the power level, may be make the cost 3 or 5 dots, drop the need to forget other contracts, and just give a flat +1 to the chosen contract's clauses for the 3 dot and a +2 for the 5 dot. Then characters can get boosts to contracts that they don't want to pump related skills in, but not have it keep growing beyond the related base dice pools.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I also post a long form story, based on a Changeling: The Lost campaign at: <a href=\"https://www.fanfiction.net/s/10018173/1/Great-Fight-A-Twilight-Tommy-Tale\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.fanfiction.net/s/1001817...ght-Tommy-Tale</a><br /> I hope you will enjoy it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2020-gitariart","name":"GitariArt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}